	</article><!-- #post-67 -->

				
					
	<article id="post-46" class="post-46 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized tag-lua tag-online-games tag-rally tag-roblox">
		<header class="entry-header">
						<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="http://pressroblox.wordpress.com/2011/07/26/over-1000-fans-worldwide-converge-on-rally-for-online-gaming-site-at-sf-exploratorium-2/" title="Permalink to Over 1,000 Fans Worldwide Converge on Rally for Online Gaming Site at SF&nbsp;Exploratorium" rel="bookmark">Over 1,000 Fans Worldwide Converge on Rally for Online Gaming Site at SF&nbsp;Exploratorium</a></h1>
			
						<div class="entry-meta">
				<span class="sep">Posted on </span><a href="http://pressroblox.wordpress.com/2011/07/26/over-1000-fans-worldwide-converge-on-rally-for-online-gaming-site-at-sf-exploratorium-2/" title="3:55 pm" rel="bookmark"><time class="entry-date" datetime="2011-07-26T15:55:42+00:00" pubdate>July 26, 2011</time></a><span class="by-author"> <span class="sep"> by </span> <span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="http://pressroblox.wordpress.com/author/pressroblox/" title="View all posts by pressroblox" rel="author">pressroblox</a></span></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->
			
						<div class="comments-link">
				<a href="http://pressroblox.wordpress.com/2011/07/26/over-1000-fans-worldwide-converge-on-rally-for-online-gaming-site-at-sf-exploratorium-2/#comments" title="Comment on Over 1,000 Fans Worldwide Converge on Rally for Online Gaming Site at SF&nbsp;Exploratorium">3</a>			</div>
					</header><!-- .entry-header -->

				<div class="entry-content">
			<p><strong>Contact for ROBLOX PR</strong><br />
Cara Porchia<br />
<a href="mailto:press@roblox.com">press@roblox.com</a><br />
415.755.8523<br />
Whitney Werth<br />
<a href="mailto:press@roblox.com">press@roblox.com</a><br />
415.595.5662</p>
<p align="center"><strong>Over 1,000 Fans Worldwide Converge on Rally for Online Gaming Site at SF Exploratorium  </strong><strong><br />
</strong><em>Sold-Out Event Teaches Kids Video Game Coding, In-Game Philanthropy, and Other Ways to Propel Future Careers </em></p>
<p><strong>SAN FRANCISCO – July 26, 2011 </strong>– ROBLOX, one of the top ranked sites on the Internet for kids, today announced it will host its first ever ROBLOX Rally at the Exploratorium in San Francisco on August 1.  The event that originally expected only 250 attendees, reached its max of 1,000 within the first two weeks of ticket sales. Kids ages 6-16 from all over the world , are traveling from as far away as England and Hong Kong to talk with ROBLOX developers, hear about the latest advancements within the game, learn how to create their own virtual worlds with LUA coding language, and share ideas about donating in-game currency, called Robux, to their favorite charity. With over 6.8 million unique visitors and 942 million page views per month and growing, ROBLOX is the second most popular kids entertainment site, behind Nickelodeon (as ranked by comScore, May 2011).</p>
<p><strong>ROBLOX Rally Details</strong><br />
Date: Monday, August 1, 2011<br />
Location: Exploratorium, 3601 Lyon St. San Francisco, CA<br />
Time: 10:00 AM- 4:00 PM<br />
Cost: $10.00, lunch included<br />
Note: The event is sold-out, only open to members of the press.</p>
<p>“We are very excited about the overwhelming response we’ve gotten for our first-ever ROBLOX Rally,” said Dave Baszucki, CEO and Founder of Roblox Corporation. “We have families coming to the Rally from as far away as Hong Kong, which is a testament to the passion and commitment kids and their parents have for ROBLOX. Parents know that kids have a lot of games to choose from and believe that ROBLOX is providing an appropriate entertainment and educational experience for their kids.”</p>
<p>ROBLOX is unique among gaming sites in that kids are the architects of the game and can learn software coding abilities that can propel future careers. Using physics to simulate the real world, ROBLOX brings the ever popular building-blocks style of play into a massively multi-player 3D game environment. Parents of ROBLOX players will also attend the event with their kids to show support for their choice to move beyond basic games and build their own 3D games. In addition to software development, ROBLOX also fosters entrepreneurism by allowing kids to become merchants of virtual goods, advertise their creations, and work collaboratively with their friends.</p>
<p>“My kids are nuts about ROBLOX, and we’re coming all the way from St. Louis to attend,” said Heather Goldman, parent of ROBLOX member. “As a software engineer, I’m very excited that my son has taken interest in creating his own games. He’s hoping to learn to script in LUA at the ROBLOX Rally.”</p>
<p><strong>Sneak-Peak of ROBLOX Rally Sessions</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>LUA Scripting 101</li>
<li>Using ROBLOX Studio and Creating Scriptable Objects</li>
<li>More New Feature Demos and Sneak Peeks</li>
<li>Design the Future of ROBLOX with David Baszucki</li>
<li>Ask a Famous ROBLOX Staff Member (almost) Anything</li>
<li>ROBLOX for Parents – Getting the most out of ROBLOX as an educational tool</li>
<li>Advanced Scripting Class – Body Animation, GUIs and AIs</li>
<li>Under the Hood – Scaling servers and databases to keep up with growth</li>
<li>Breaking Into the Software Industry – The interns tell you how!</li>
<li>Advanced Scripting Class – Body Animation, GUIs and AIs</li>
</ul>
<p>For more information and a complete Rally schedule, visit: <a href="http://blog.roblox.com/?p=5340" target="_blank">http://blog.roblox.com/?p=5340</a></p>
<p><strong>Press release</strong>: <a href="http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20110726005774/en/1000-Fans-Worldwide-Converge-Rally-Online-Gaming">http://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20110726005774/en/1000-Fans-Worldwide-Converge-Rally-Online-Gaming</a></p>
<p><strong>ROBLOX is Hiring. </strong>For more information, visit:  <a href="http://jobs.roblox.com/" target="_blank">jobs.roblox.com</a><strong><br />
</strong></p>
<p><strong>About ROBLOX</strong></p>
<p>ROBLOX is one of the top-ranked kids gaming sites on the Internet. With over 6.8 million unique visitors each month, ROBLOX is unique among gaming sites because users are the architects of their own worlds. ROBLOX is a massively multi-player 3D game environment with tens of thousands of games that use physics to simulate the real world, and a virtual economy with millions of highly customized characters. Players on ROBLOX demonstrate incredible creativity limited only by their imagination, using core building components to create their own elaborate online games, social hangouts, and custom virtual items.</p>
<p>For more information, visit <a href="http://www.roblox.com/" target="_blank">www.roblox.com</a></p>
<div class="sharedaddy sd-sharing-enabled"></div>					</div><!-- .entry-content -->
		
